Kubernetes Services
Service is a method for exposing Pods in your cluster.
Each Pod gets its own IP address, but we need access using the Node IP.
To access Pods internally within the cluster, we use ClusterIP.
If the Service type is NodePort or LoadBalancer, it can also be accessed from outside the cluster.
Services help decouple Pods from the network topology, making applications easier to manage and scale.
Types of Kubernetes Services
   ClusterIP
   NodePort
   LoadBalancer
